to Pokemon as just like a  franchise because I think it's really  fun and creative  [Music]  he moved to LA and worked on the film  for seven months doing concept art for  characters and the environments  he helped come up with the initial  designs for the pokemons  and then you know it gets given to like  all sorts of crazy effects house while  his Pokemon on deviantART are more  realistic the ones he designed for the  film had to be a bit more traditional  you know excite working on the movie  like they had to get a more inline with  the cartoon aesthetic I think you do a  design and then people have opinions and  then you do another design and they  he'll also still have opinions and you  know so it's just like a constant back  and forth of trying to make you know one  person happy which you know is gonna  make somebody else unhappy and then you  have to try and find a middle ground  that's gonna work for people  Pikachu as the star of the film and  franchise took a while to nail down and  get right Pikachu is like one of the  most well known cartoon characters ever  right despite speaking English and being  a bit more furry than the cartoon the  Pikachu in the film is different from  his realistic design I based him on  rodents and lagomorph slag remorse or  like rabbits just like you know like  small woodland critters but it was mr.  mime that really grabbed the Internet's  attention since his debut in the trailer  he's become a meme mr. mime was always  gonna be weird right because what do you  make that thing when I did my realistic  version of it I made out of frog because  like it can be so many weird things I  think a detail that I didn't you know  know they were gonna go for but when  they like the the little shoulder  pauldrons actually look like kick balls  I thought that was a pretty fun idea and  the jigglypuff I like in the Pokedex  injuries they talked about it having a  balloon-like skin texture which would  probably be pretty creepy in real life  